course: dictionary
lesson: 3461
title: Faintly: weak, quiet, or a little
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Music played faintly in the distance.» You cannot hear the music clearly, so faintly must mean weakly or quietly. The word «distance» is a clue too: sounds from far away are often faint.
explain: Faintly can also mean a little, as in «faintly surprised». The word tells you the surprise was small, not big. Check the words around it, then try the swap test: put "a little" or "quietly" in place of faintly and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In Toad's story, «at intervals he faintly murmured "Poop-poop!"». Murmured means said softly, so faintly fits: he spoke quietly. «He only smiled faintly» tells you his smile was small and slight.
fact: Faintly is an adverb, a word that tells how something is done or how much.
fact: «Faintly» means weakly, quietly or not clearly, so it is hard to see, hear or smell.
fact: «Faintly» can also mean slightly or a little, as in «faintly surprised».
fact: The opposites of faintly are strongly, loudly and clearly.
fact: «Placid» means calm, so Toad's face was calm when he faintly murmured.
exercise: «Music played faintly in the distance.» What does faintly mean? | *Quietly, so it is hard to hear | Loudly, so everyone could hear | Happily and dancing | Very fast
exercise: Which word is closest to the opposite of faintly? | Gently | Slowly | *Strongly | Sleepily
exercise: «his face wore a placid satisfied expression» Find and copy one word that means calm. | expression | *placid | wore | satisfied
test: «The house smelled faintly of smoke.» What does faintly tell the reader? | The smoke is green | *Something is weak, or only a little | Something is very strong | The house is on fire
test: In which sentence does faintly mean a little? | «The bell rang faintly across the field.» | *«She felt faintly sleepy after lunch.» | «The lamp glowed faintly in the dark.» | «The band played faintly, far away.»
exam: Toad «at intervals he faintly murmured "Poop-poop!"» What does faintly most likely mean here? | *Quietly and weakly, so the words were hard to hear | Happily singing a song | Angrily and loudly | Wrongly, with the wrong words
